uuid":"6cb281a5-1fd7-42e0-bd7d-879c6878893d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9cd6-4652-f8f2-4879"},{"link_uuid":"e70eec8d-5b4f-43d1-a06c-4e84b3bb208e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1971-6992-491c-41c2"},{"link_uuid":"52dc4ba8-66ef-4359-a6f5-efa97d86c5fa","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8643-6951-b967-4b14"},{"link_uuid":"1d5c8b2c-7522-47fb-bb5d-2636321ef803","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3286-21d2-1c53-4cc2"},{"link_uuid":"afa19189-159d-48e4-8f3d-92bbc5376a35","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a1af-386e-ae26-444c"},{"link_uuid":"94d2e01e-b455-4635-b7ce-8bf18d2ef1cb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"114d-761d-bab6-4e2a"},{"link_uuid":"b9f3edda-a746-4b1d-81ab-5d151b42d8c8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"645c-ec16-af1c-45df"},{"link_uuid":"334ae881-1134-4511-8b5e-67c57096ad9f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"778c-ec65-e745-42fc"},{"link_uuid":"8af618db-d388-4c9d-8761-2a52c840b875","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0711-ae28-5277-464b"},{"link_uuid":"df2283bf-1735-4a17-bf62-aa460898d00b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a4b1-ca1e-9ea2-4804"},{"link_uuid":"404d1653-2645-4241-8060-f767d01c5b82","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"371e-8eea-bd5c-4a66"},{"link_uuid":"44a55d0d-af48-4943-8f86-9c9379886dba","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d176-d42a-e30d-425e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen Python modules under `tests/unit` contain 36 audited prose blocks: 26 true leading docstrings and 10 full-line comment regions. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45`. The old ranges included helpers, fixtures, constants, and assertions and split several logical comment regions; the stable IDs own only actual prose. Current source uses `verify-identity` and the `gate_context.current_code_sha` seam, which remain executable and protected.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the stable-ID blocks below. For every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_detached_drain_child_survives_removal_of_the_spawning_worktree`\n- `tests/unit/test_divergence_grade_split.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_RECORDED_BINARY = {`\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_doctor_cli_mcp_client_scan_is_hermetic`\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_mcp_client.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py`: `D:test_engine_submodules_resolve_when_the_tests_unit_shadow_is_active`\n- `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py` — 6 blocks:\n  - `C:repo:before:monkeypatch.setenv(\"REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_DRAIN\", \"off\")`\n  - `D:test_backlog_drains_despite_a_low_sorted_churn_set`\n  - `D:test_overlap_drain_is_read_from_the_llm_table`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _drain_lock(repo: str) -> Path:`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _canonical_store(tmp_path: Path) -> str:`\n  - `D:test_reenrich_debounce_bounds_the_self_heal_fanout`\n- `tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py` — 6 blocks:\n  - `C:<module>:before:_BASE_NS = 1_700_000_000_000_000_000  # a realistic fixed-width ns stamp (Nov 2023)`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _count_reductions(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> list[str]:`\n  - `D:test_gate_marker_lives_outside_the_tracker`\n  - `D:test_existence_probe_cost_does_not_scale_with_the_backlog`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _canonical_store(tmp_path: Path) -> str:`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_standing_backlog_probe_scales_with_backlog_not_store(`\n- `tests/unit/test_ensures_boot_budget_e43f.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding_isolation.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:_reimportable`\n- `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py` — 3 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_every_env_reading_llm_helper_is_registered_at_the_right_position`\n  - `D:test_dropping_a_used_helpers_row_fails_loudly_instead_of_shrinking`\n- `tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_screen_warm_call_provider_error_propagates(rebar_repo: Path) -> None:`\n- `tests/unit/test_error_code_insecure_url_7d6a.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_error_handling_convention.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:test_every_packaged_spec_passes_strict_validation`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_TWO_UNMET_CASE = {\"expect\": \"fail\", \"expected_unmet_criteria\": [\"AC1\", \"AC2\"]}`\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_solver_project_criterion.py`: `D:<module>`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is one maximal full-line comment region anchored to unchanged code. No other prose is editable. In reviewer TSV, `stable_block_id` is the path-qualified `<path>#<D:...>` or `<path>#<C:...>` value.\n\n## Protected false positives\nAll unlisted prose and every executable/directive line are protected. This includes inline queue timestamp rationale, exact subprocess arguments, current import seams, test data, and concise unrelated docstrings in the large enrichment/doctor modules.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Measurement/divergence prose keeps held-out boundaries, grade distinctions, recorded regression attributes, and advisory wiring.\n- Detached/doctor/engine prose keeps durable child CWD, dirty-store healing, mapping and MCP-client diagnostics, hermetic HOME injection, and subprocess proof against test-package shadowing.\n- Enrichment prose keeps fairness, config-table ownership, lock reclaim/canonicalization, debounce, bounded reductions, O(1) probes, scoped markers, and counted-not-timed evidence.\n- Ensure/env prose keeps bounded boot, module-binding restoration, current canonical tracker lookup, complete helper registration, and loud generator failure.\n- Epic/error/eval prose keeps fail-closed provider screening, distinct insecure-URL classification, Ruff-gate teeth, strict packaged-spec coverage, all-unmet scoring, and project-criterion reverse resolution.\n- All modules are direct pytest inputs. `test_ensures_late_binding_isolation.py` imports its owned sibling; the eval workflow selects `test_eval_scorers.py`; spawn/relocation, suite-isolation, and env-registry tests are path/source consumers. No target `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Prose changes occur only inside the 36 declared stable-ID blocks.\n- [ ] Any changed blank line is adjacent to an edited stable-ID block.\n- [ ] The normalized-AST comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] The token/comment comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 36 leaf-linked TSV rows, one for each declared stable-ID block.\n- [ ] Every reviewer row uses this schema: stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session.\n- [ ] Every before_citation equals 9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every final_citation equals <final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every row records after_words < before_words.\n- [ ] Every row records directives_exact=PASS.\n- [ ] Every row records semantic-preservation=PASS, confirming its preserved_contract_or_consumer.\n- [ ] Every row records bloat-removal=PASS, confirming removal of chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest (including real consumers), scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance_heldout.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_divergence_grade_split.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_mcp_client.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ensures_boot_budget_e43f.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding_isolation.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_error_code_insecure_url_7d6a.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_error_handling_convention.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_eval_solver_project_criterion.py","reason":"Condense audited prose while preserving the pinned current contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","ae4d-df34-480d-4c88"],["relates_to","323e-e5d3-dbd6-4d4a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","parent_status_uuid":"5c39fea5-13c1-4eb2-8e11-635beb486db2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"029a-c2e8-b4af-44db","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 10: det_measurement_provenance_heldout–eval_solver_project_criterion","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance_heldout.py tests/unit/test